# Track q3kgroups: on the default 1017 Q3_K_M file the V4.1 prompt batch runs a Q3_K q_b with no
# indexer query, and the Q3_K kv of a ratio-1 compressor source, as the joined path's one column-group
# launch a sub-block (Gpu::enqueue_gemv_q3k_groups) again, where 1dd382876 ran them through the step's
# m-column launcher a chunk at a time (a quantize_q8_1 and an enqueue_m a chunk). The groups launcher
# is bit for bit enqueue_gemv_q3k on each group's columns (its contract), so bits do not move; only the
# launch count does (AGENTS.md change class "launch count only").
#
# Decomposition [derived, from weekly-gpu-ds41-flowcounts' 2026-11-15 counts at --place gate, P = 512
# and 1536]: a full sub-block of 16 chunks issues 2 x 16 = 32 launches for one arm where the groups
# path issues 1: +31, four sub-blocks a full layer-batch, so +124 route entries on each of the 30
# layers without an indexer (layer 20's ratio-1 kv source counts the same) and +63 / +32 / +1 on the
# tail layers 37 / 38 / 39; at P = 4096 that is ~8 x (27..30 x 124 + 96) = 27,500..30,500 entries a
# call, the size of the enqthread cut (26,344). Host: an entry costs t_e ~2.4..3.0 us of issue
# (enqthread replay) -> 66..92 ms a call. Card: each removed launch also removes its launch gap
# (~0.9 us a node, the flow model's gap) -> 25..28 ms; the weight bytes do not change (the groups
# kernel reads the rows once a group, as the chunked launches did). With the launch queue at 2x in
# both arms (the variable set, so the lqdefault default does not differ between them) the host's
# back-pressure is small and most of the issue term is on the chain: chain -0.4..-1.0 %
# (35..85 ms of a ~8.4 s prompt call).
# Resource timeline per layer-batch: host thread enqueue ~4.1 (at 2x) + union 30.2, a sum; card
# ~33..34 under it. The cut shortens the host's enqueue term and the card's gaps; neither is under the
# other's shadow while the host and card each hold the chain in turn.
kind: ab
question: does running the two unjoined Q3_K arms as one column-group launch a sub-block again
  shorten the V4.1 prompt call by their issue and launch-gap time?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose, depth 0, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 Q3_K_M, --place a, the default
  levers (group 2, residency and host streaming on), CUDA_SCALE_LAUNCH_QUEUES=2x in both arms,
  RTX A6000 - (this tree - base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +0.4..+1.0
rounds: 8
sd: 0.25 % the lead's 2026-11-15 cardexp sitting (A6000, place a, prose P = 4096, 3f018b518 against 4e28e0a54), the pp ratio's per-round SD 0.35 % over 8 rounds over sqrt 2 for one run
condition: this tree's generate_ds41 and main 6cf1d24c2's (/root/repo/bloomery's build, a bin: arm)
  alternate in one lease, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=8 just depth-gpu-ds41
  prose:4096@BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1,CUDA_SCALE_LAUNCH_QUEUES=2x
  bin:/root/repo/bloomery/target/release/generate_ds41:prose:4096@BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1,CUDA_SCALE_LAUNCH_QUEUES=2x,
  the order rotated every round; both arms' plan prints name the same residency word and
  card_experts; in every round the stat lines read: this tree's entries_route 90..125 a
  layer-batch under the base's, entries_shadow equal across arms (counts: a binary that does not
  show them is not the tree's), union_lb within 0.5 ms of the base's, enqueue_lb 0.2..0.4 ms under
  it; no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: land the train (this cut with the launch-queue default); weekly-gpu-ds41-flowcounts goes
  green on the next weekly with no flow model change
decide-below: entries_route fell as predicted but pp did not move: the removed launches were under
  the card's shadow; land for the counts alone (the flowcounts pin) and record the term as 0
decide-above: the chunked launches cost the card more than their gaps (card_in_lb fell more than
  0.5 ms a layer-batch): the groups kernel shares weight reads across groups through L2; price that
  term in the flow model's constants before the next attention change
# outcome 2026-11-15 (one lease, A6000 300 W 2100 MHz, fbd58dc9b's generate_ds41 against 6cf1d24c2's, both arms
#  CUDA_SCALE_LAUNCH_QUEUES=2x, 8 rounds, order rotated, no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row): pp this tree / base per round
#  r1 1.2178 [cold, both arms] r2 1.0582 (the base arm's 467.16 still warming) r3..r8 1.0018 1.0035 1.0055 1.0029 1.0049
#  1.0073; the runner's mean over all 8 is 1.0378 +- 0.0629 (r1, r2 inside it); over the warm rounds r3..r8 +0.43 % +- 0.21 %
#  (t 2.571, 5 df): in band, at its low edge. Decode @ 4096 1.0010 +- 0.0059 (unmoved). Stat lines: this tree's
#  entries_route 410 / 1306 on layers 0 / 1 (the flow model's values) against the base's 534 / 1430. decide-in: landed with
#  the launch-queue default (fbd58dc9b); the issue and gap terms are where the card put them.
